-- title:
--   Fixed numerical rich sources have mesh-independent scalar data
-- statement:
--   Let $M_0,M_1$ be any two regular meshes with positive lower parameters. Suppose they carry fixed-rich-source witnesses for exactly the same numerical parameters $c,\delta_*,\beta_{\rm prot},\beta_{\rm act}$, source-cell margin, depth, tail threshold, cutoff, rough level, exponent, and guarded tail family $F$. At each source use its prescribed balanced alpha and the common extended guarded smooth base mass from $F$. Eventually, for every proof that the ambient index exceeds the tail threshold,
--
--   $$m_{\rm frozen}^{(0)}=m_{\rm frozen}^{(1)},\qquad\mathrm{logY}^{(0)}=\mathrm{logY}^{(1)},\qquad\Lambda_{0,\rm rounded}^{(0)}=\Lambda_{0,\rm rounded}^{(1)}.$$
--
--   The theorem compares local formulas directly, enabling a scalar ledger chosen on one mesh to be reused on another.
